PART 2: UNDERSTANDING COLOR STATE
================================================================================

WHAT IS COLOR STATE?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Color state is:

• A state variable storing the current color

• Updated dynamically in response to application actions

• Used to control visual properties

• Coordinated with quote changes

• Stored as a string

Examples:

'#667eea'

'rgb(102, 126, 234)'

'purple'


• Preserved across component re-renders

• Updated using its state setter

• Passed to child components through props when needed


