================================================================================
STEP 3: CREATE getRandomColor()
================================================================================

const getRandomColor = () => {

  const randomIndex =
    Math.floor(
      Math.random() *
      COLORS.length
    )


  return COLORS[randomIndex]
}


HOW IT WORKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose:

COLORS.length = 10


Math.random()

returns a value:

0 <= n < 1


Example:

0.63


Multiply:

0.63 × 10
=
6.3


Math.floor(6.3)

=
6


Then:

COLORS[6]

returns the color stored at index 6.


FUNCTION EXPLANATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+
| CODE                         | PURPOSE                                 |
+------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+
| getRandomColor()             | Defines helper function                 |
| Math.random()                | Returns random decimal >= 0 and < 1    |
| * COLORS.length              | Scales number to palette length         |
| Math.floor(...)              | Converts value to integer index         |
| COLORS[randomIndex]          | Returns selected color                  |
+------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+


RANDOM COLOR FLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Math.random()
     ↓
Random Decimal
     ↓
× COLORS.length
     ↓
Scaled Value
     ↓
Math.floor()
     ↓
Array Index
     ↓
COLORS[index]
     ↓
Random Color


================================================================================
IMPORTANT: RANDOM DOES NOT GUARANTEE A DIFFERENT COLOR
================================================================================

This:

getRandomColor()

selects a random color.

It does NOT guarantee that the selected color differs from the current color.

Example:

Current:

#667eea


Random selection:

#667eea


Result:

The quote changes but the visual color appears unchanged.


IF A DIFFERENT COLOR IS REQUIRED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const getDifferentRandomColor = (
  currentColor
) => {

  if (COLORS.length <= 1) {
    return COLORS[0]
  }


  let nextColor =
    currentColor


  while (
    nextColor === currentColor
  ) {

    const randomIndex =
      Math.floor(
        Math.random() *
        COLORS.length
      )


    nextColor =
      COLORS[randomIndex]
  }


  return nextColor
}


Then:

setColor(currentColor =>
  getDifferentRandomColor(
    currentColor
  )
)


