================================================================================
ASYNC STATE COORDINATION
================================================================================

const handleAction = async () => {

  setLoading(true)

  setError(null)


  try {

    const data =
      await fetchData()


    setQuote(data)


    setColor(
      getRandomColor()
    )

  } catch (err) {

    setError(
      err.message
    )

  } finally {

    setLoading(false)

  }
}


================================================================================
STATE COORDINATION PATTERNS
================================================================================

+------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
| PATTERN                | USE WHEN                                     |
+------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
| Sequential Logic       | Later calculation depends on earlier result  |
| Independent Updates    | States don't depend on each other            |
| Conditional Update     | State changes only under condition           |
| Batched Processing     | Multiple setters occur together              |
| Async Update           | State depends on async result                |
| Loading State          | Track request progress                       |
| Error State            | Track request failure                        |
| Reset                  | Return state to known initial values         |
+------------------------+----------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
WHEN SHOULD MULTIPLE STATE VALUES BE GROUPED?
================================================================================

Separate state is appropriate when values represent independent concerns.

Example:

quote

color

loading

error


Grouping everything is NOT automatically better.

You might consider useReducer or grouped state when:

• State transitions become complicated

• Many setters always change together

• One action has several related transition rules

• State logic becomes difficult to maintain


================================================================================
BEST PRACTICES FOR MULTIPLE STATE VALUES
================================================================================

• Use descriptive names

• Keep state minimal

• Keep unrelated concerns separate when useful

• Use functional updates when next state depends on previous state

• Handle loading and error states explicitly

• Avoid unnecessary prop drilling

• Pass only data required by child components

• Avoid duplicating derived values

• Move constants outside components when possible

• Consider useReducer when transitions become complex

• Test behavior rather than internal setter calls


