================================================================================
COLOR ACCESSIBILITY
================================================================================

Random color selection introduces an important requirement:

READABILITY.


A visually attractive random color may not provide sufficient contrast
against:

• White text
• Dark text
• Buttons
• Icons


Example:

Very light yellow:

#fee140

with white text may be harder to read than a darker background.


PRACTICAL OPTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Curate the palette so every color works with the foreground text

• Store a corresponding foreground color with each background

• Calculate/select an appropriate text color

• Provide a high-contrast theme

• Test actual color combinations


BETTER COLOR MODEL EXAMPLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const THEMES = [

  {
    background: '#667eea',
    foreground: '#ffffff'
  },

  {
    background: '#fee140',
    foreground: '#212529'
  }

]


Then state could store a theme:

const [theme, setTheme] =
  useState(THEMES[0])


Use:

style={{
  backgroundColor:
    theme.background,

  color:
    theme.foreground
}}


